+          "claim": "Well order the point-finite cover. For $x\\in X$ let $$\\rho_x=\\sup\\{r>0:B(x,r)\\subseteq C_\\alpha \\text{ for some }\\alpha\\}.$$ Put $m_x=\\min\\{1,\\rho_x/4\\}$ when $\\rho_x<\\infty$, and $m_x=1$ otherwise. Then $0<m_x\\le1$ and $B(x,2m_x)$ lies in some cover member: its radius is strictly below $\\rho_x$. Assign $x$ to the first $C_\\alpha$ containing $B(x,2m_x)$, and let $C'_\\alpha$ be the union of all $B(x,m_x)$ assigned to $\\alpha$. [A1, F1, construct]",
