+          "claim": "Fix $x\\in X$ and a neighbourhood $N$ of $x$ meeting only $A_{i_1},\\ldots,A_{i_n}$. Choose an open neighbourhood $O$ of $x$ with $O\\subseteq N$. If $O\\cap\\overline{A_j}\\ne\\varnothing$, choose $y\\in O\\cap\\overline{A_j}$; the open neighbourhood $O$ of $y$ then meets $A_j$, so $N$ meets $A_j$ and $j\\in\\{i_1,\\ldots,i_n\\}$. [F1, L1]",
+          "step": "1.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "F1",
+            "L1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "step-1-2",
+          "claim": "The inclusion $\\bigcup_i\\overline{A_i}\\subseteq\\overline{\\bigcup_iA_i}$ holds because each $\\overline{A_i}$ is contained in every closed set containing $A_i$, in particular in $\\overline{\\bigcup_iA_i}$. [L1]",
+          "step": "1.2",
+          "inputs": [
+            "L1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "step-2-1",
+          "claim": "Thus $O$ meets only $\\overline{A_{i_1}},\\ldots,\\overline{A_{i_n}}$, so the closed family is locally finite. [step 1.1, F1]",
+          "step": "2.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "1.1",
+            "F1"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
