+          "claim": "Let $x\\in\\overline{\\bigcup_iA_i}$ and take $N$ as in step 1.1; if $x\\notin\\bigcup_i\\overline{A_i}$, then for each $i_k$ an open neighbourhood of $x$ misses $A_{i_k}$, and its finite intersection with an open neighbourhood inside $N$ misses every $A_i$, contradicting the closure criterion. [step 1.1, L1]",
