+          "claim": "Fix $x$. If $C'_\\alpha$ meets $B(x,m_x/8)$, choose a ball $B(y,m_y)\\subseteq C'_\\alpha$ meeting it. We claim $x\\in C_\\alpha$. Otherwise $x\\notin B(y,2m_y)$, while intersection gives $d(x,y)<m_y+m_x/8$; hence $m_y<m_x/8\\le1/8$. Thus the truncation in step 1.1 is inactive at $y$ and $\\rho_y=4m_y$. But $$B(y,5m_y)\\subseteq B(x,2m_x),$$ because $d(x,y)+5m_y<6m_y+m_x/8<7m_x/8$; the right-hand ball lies in some cover member by step 1.1. This contradicts the definition of $\\rho_y$. Thus $x\\in C_\\alpha$. [step 1.1]",
