research/audit/wave0-linear-algebra.provenance.jsonl:{"id":"fs-union-of-two-subspaces-is-a-subspace","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://linear.axler.net/LADR4e.pdf","https://www.andreaminini.net/math/the-union-of-vector-subspaces"],"rationale":"The false claim and the exact condition in the Remarks are Axler 4e Exercise 1C.12 verbatim: 'Prove that the union of two subspaces of V is a subspace of V if and only if one of the subspaces is contained in the other', together with Axler's margin note 'The union of subspaces is rarely a subspace (see Exercise 12)'. The refuting construction, the two coordinate axes of the plane with (1,0) + (0,1) = (1,1) outside their union, is located in Andrea Minini, The union of vector subspaces. Delta: stated over an arbitrary field rather than R, and packaged as a false-statement item with the criterion moved to the Remarks. Refutation written locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}
