research/audit/wave1-combinatorics.provenance.jsonl:{"id":"fs-the-erdos-szekeres-bound-can-be-lowered","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erd%C5%91s%E2%80%93Szekeres_theorem"],"rationale":"The false statement is the standard Erdos-Szekeres theorem with the sharp length mn+1 lowered to mn. The source supplies both the true bound and its sharpness, so this is a recoverable alteration, not a novel claim. The refutation instantiates the standard sharpness construction and adds the local zero-parameter diagnosis.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-02"}

