+          "claim": "For every $x\\in F$, Hausdorffness gives disjoint open sets $U,V$ with $x\\in U$ and $p\\in V$; hence $p\\notin\\overline U$, since $X\\setminus V$ is closed and contains $U$. Thus the family of all open $U$ with $U\\cap F\\ne\\varnothing$ and $p\\notin\\overline U$, together with $X\\setminus F$, is an open cover $\\mathcal U$ of $X$. [F1, construct]",
