+{"id":"def-cover-refinement-and-local-finiteness","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paracompact_space"],"rationale":"The sources give the standard definitions of refinement, local finiteness, point-finiteness, and star refinement. The item combines them into one convention ledger and uses a point-star notation rather than reproducing one source verbatim; the mathematical notions and directions agree.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-locally-finite-unions-and-closures","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math443b.pdf"],"rationale":"Rice topology notes §5.13.2 state that closures of a locally finite family remain locally finite and that closure commutes with its union; the closed-union conclusion is the stated specialization. The local proof expands the standard neighbourhood argument in different prose.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"def-paracompact-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"The notes use exactly the library convention: every open cover has a locally finite open refining cover, with Hausdorffness not built into the definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"prop-compact-spaces-are-paracompact","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"The source states under the same non-Hausdorff convention that every compact space is paracompact. The proof is the standard finite-subcover argument, rewritten locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"prop-closed-subspaces-of-paracompact-spaces","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"Munkres §41, Theorem 41.2, states exactly that every closed subspace of a paracompact space is paracompact. The item supplies the usual ambient-cover/traces proof in local notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-paracompact-hausdorff-is-regular","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.csun.edu/~ac53971/research/topology_262.pdf"],"rationale":"The University of Chicago topology notes prove that a paracompact Hausdorff space is regular by the same locally finite refinement and closure-of-union construction. The item separates Hausdorffness from the local paracompactness convention and rewrites the proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"thm-paracompact-hausdorff-implies-normal","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"Munkres §41, Theorem 41.1, states exactly that every paracompact Hausdorff space is normal. The proof is a standard closed-set separation argument adapted to the library's separate regularity lemma.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"def-partition-of-unity-subordinate-to-a-cover","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.wisc.edu/~jwrobbin/partitions_of_unity.pdf","https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources define partitions by continuous [0,1]-valued functions summing to one with locally finite supports and define subordination by support containment. The item instead requires local finiteness of cozero sets; for such a family the closure lemma makes the support family locally finite, and the converse is immediate. This is an equivalent convention delta.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-algebra-of-continuous-real-maps-on-a-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math443b.pdf","https://math.berkeley.edu/~giventh/10415.html"],"rationale":"The university sources record continuity of arithmetic operations on real-valued continuous maps; absolute value and binary max/min follow by the displayed standard formulas, finite nonempty versions by iteration, and division is restricted to the nonzero-denominator subspace. The item merges these established closure rules into one statement and supplies its own epsilon proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-locally-finite-sums-are-continuous","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math443b.pdf"],"rationale":"Rice §5.14.1 gives the same locally finite-sum theorem for arbitrary continuous real-valued functions. The item specializes to nonnegative functions whose cozero family is locally finite and rewrites the identical local finite-sum argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-normalizing-a-locally-finite-positive-family","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math443b.pdf"],"rationale":"Rice §5.14.2 gives the same positive locally finite family, continuous sum, normalization psi_l=phi_l/Phi, unchanged positivity sets, and sum-one conclusion. The item adds the immediate support-equality consequence and uses the library's cozero terminology.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-paracompact-hausdorff-cover-shrinking","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.csun.edu/~ac53971/research/topology_262.pdf","https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the shrinking lemma and the iterated chain of locally finite covers with closure containment. The item exposes the normally implicit Choice used to retain cover assignments and reindexes the two applications, so it is a faithful semantic alteration rather than an exact transcription.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"thm-subordinate-partitions-of-unity-exist","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.csun.edu/~ac53971/research/topology_262.pdf","https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-41.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources prove existence of a subordinate partition on a paracompact Hausdorff space by shrinking, Urysohn functions, a locally finite positive sum, and normalization. The item makes Choice and Dependent Choice explicit and uses cozero-local-finiteness, which are convention/foundational deltas.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"thm-partitions-of-unity-characterize-paracompact-hausdorff-spaces","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.wisc.edu/~jwrobbin/partitions_of_unity.pdf"],"rationale":"Robbin states that a Hausdorff space admits partitions subordinate to every open cover iff it is paracompact. The item makes the sufficient Choice/DC assumptions explicit and uses the equivalent locally finite cozero convention; its reverse proof extracts the cozero refinement.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"cor-compact-hausdorff-partitions-of-unity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.csun.edu/~ac53971/research/topology_262.pdf","https://www.uni-math.gwdg.de/tammo/GT01.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give finite-cover partitions on normal spaces and the relabel-and-sum construction that groups a locally finite partition over a finite target cover. Compact Hausdorff implies normal in the standard setting; the item makes Choice/DC explicit and packages the result as a compact-Hausdorff corollary.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-metric-open-covers-have-point-finite-refinements","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.ams.org/proc/1969-021-02/"],"rationale":"Ornstein's primary two-page paper, part (A), constructs from a well-ordered metric open cover the same dyadic-ball point-finite open refinement. The item modernizes notation, makes Choice explicit, and expands the coverage and ordinal-descent checks.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
+{"id":"lem-metric-point-finite-refinements-can-be-made-locally-finite","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.ams.org/proc/1969-021-02/"],"rationale":"Ornstein's part (B) starts with the point-finite cover from part (A), assigns controlled-radius balls to first eligible members, and proves local finiteness by the same small-ball test. The item separates the upgrade as a lemma, makes Choice explicit, and rewrites the constants and details.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
