+          "claim": "We first prove a one-shrink construction for any open cover $\\mathcal C$. Let $\\mathcal R$ be the family of all open $R$ for which $\\overline R\\subseteq C$ for some $C\\in\\mathcal C$. By [L1], $\\mathcal R$ covers $X$. Take a locally finite open refining cover $\\mathcal A$ of $\\mathcal R$ by [F1], discard its empty members, and use [A1] to assign to each $A\\in\\mathcal A$ sets $R(A)\\in\\mathcal R$ and $C(A)\\in\\mathcal C$ with $$A\\subseteq R(A)\\subseteq\\overline{R(A)}\\subseteq C(A).$$ Then $\\overline A\\subseteq\\overline{R(A)}\\subseteq C(A)$. [A1, L1, F1, construct]",
